WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:07.290
At 20, one in three people already has this on their MRI, and it does not hurt at all.

2
00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:13.170
Many people believe that if the MRI says hernia, protrusion or disc degeneration, that is the cause of their pain.

3
00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.170
But look at this study.

4
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:19.850
37% at 20 years old, 96% at 80. Without pain.

5
00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.850
It is true. It is an injury.

6
00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:24.250
The wear of walking on two legs for a lifetime.

7
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.290
But its being there does not mean it is the cause of your pain.

8
00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:29.490
Imaging tests are complementary tests.

9
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:34.010
The clinical picture leads, unless there is a fracture, loss of strength or a warning sign.

10
00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.810
Then, yes, the image leads, but always together with the clinical picture.

